<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<%- include('partials/html-head'); -%>
	<body>
		<div id="app" class="wrap prose" v-cloak>
			<%- include('partials/header', { heading: 'Privacy policy' }); -%>

			<section>
				<h3>What We Collect</h3>
				<p>
					When you create an account, we collect your email address and your chosen username. When you send
					notifications, we store the message content temporarily. If you @mention other users, they receive your notification, and they
					can see its content and your username. We also collect technical information like IP
					addresses for security and service reliability. Our servers keep standard access logs (such as IP address,
					request time, and requested URL), but these logs <strong>never</strong> include the contents of your push
					notifications.
				</p>

				<h3>How Long We Keep Your Data</h3>
				<p>
					Notifications are automatically deleted after <strong>24 hours</strong>. Access logs are automatically cleared
					after <strong>8 days</strong>. Your account information (email,
					username, settings) is kept as long as your account is active. If you delete your account, all data is
					permanently removed within 7 days.
				</p>

				<h3>How We Use Your Data</h3>
				<p>
					We use your data only to provide the Pushie service: delivering notifications and maintaining your account. We
					do not sell or rent your personal information. We share data only with the service providers listed below, and
					only as needed to run the service. We do not use your notifications for marketing, analytics, or any purpose
					beyond delivery.
				</p>

				<h3>Third-Party Services</h3>
				<p>Pushie relies on a few third parties to work:</p>
				<ul>
					<li>
						<strong>Browser push services</strong> (Google, Apple, Mozilla, or whichever provider your browser uses):
						notifications are delivered to your devices through these services, so they receive your notification
						content, which is encrypted for your device, along with technical details of your device subscription.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Amazon Web Services (AWS)</strong>: we use AWS to send account-related emails, such as email
						verification and password resets. AWS receives your email address and the content of those emails.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Cabin</strong>: we use Cabin Analytics to collect aggregated usage statistics about how Pushie is
						used. It is not used to read or analyze your notifications.
					</li>
				</ul>
				<p>These providers handle data under their own privacy policies.</p>

				<h3>Security</h3>
				<p>
					We encrypt data in transit using industry-standard TLS. Notifications are stored securely and automatically
					deleted after 24 hours. However, no system is perfectly secure. Keep your account credentials confidential.
				</p>

				<h3>Your Rights</h3>
				<p>
					You can access, update, or delete your account anytime through your settings. Deleted accounts have all data
					removed within 7 days.
				</p>

				<h3>Changes to This Policy</h3>
				<p>
					We may update this privacy policy anytime. Significant changes will be announced via email or on our website.
					Your continued use means you accept the updated policy.
				</p>

				<h3>Contact</h3>
				<p>Questions about your privacy? Email us at <a href="mailto:hello@pushie.net">hello@pushie.net</a>.</p>
			</section>
		</div>
		<%- include('partials/footer'); -%>
	</body>
</html>
